WEBVTT

00:02:23.420 --> 00:02:26.050
Hey, what's wrong?

00:02:26.590 --> 00:02:29.290
Hey...

00:02:38.500 --> 00:02:40.060
Big brother...

00:02:50.350 --> 00:02:52.050
Where are you off to?

00:02:52.050 --> 00:02:55.110
I'm gonna give food to the fish in the pond.

00:02:55.390 --> 00:02:57.120
This is no time for that, is it?!

00:02:58.460 --> 00:03:00.750
Are you aware of what you've done?

00:03:05.330 --> 00:03:07.560
No... No...

00:03:07.700 --> 00:03:11.640
What have you done to me? Everything's come to naught.

00:03:11.800 --> 00:03:16.330
I only did what Granddad told me. And big brother, even you...

00:03:16.570 --> 00:03:19.910
If you think about his age, there are limits, right?

00:03:19.910 --> 00:03:22.140
I'm just a dummy.

00:03:53.610 --> 00:03:55.840
Kazamatsuri has taken over the company?

00:03:57.750 --> 00:03:59.720
It appears that at an emergency meeting of the board of directors,

00:03:59.720 --> 00:04:04.610
...a motion to dismiss the president and certain executives was presented and carried, my lady.

00:04:05.360 --> 00:04:10.980
Not surprisingly, every one of the newly appointed persons is in Kazamatsuri's fold.

00:04:12.900 --> 00:04:19.440
He also seems to be assembling the Blattaria in the Core Settlement.

00:04:19.440 --> 00:04:21.510
With both financial might and military might in his hands,

00:04:21.510 --> 00:04:24.840
...I wonder if he's thinking of becoming a latter-day imperialist or some such?

00:04:31.280 --> 00:04:33.720
Sorry! It's me. It's Toru, Ma'am!

00:04:40.560 --> 00:04:43.460
Um, could you come to the infirmary right away?

00:04:43.900 --> 00:04:45.620
Has something happened?

00:04:46.100 --> 00:04:47.260
Kiyoko is...

00:04:58.910 --> 00:05:02.450
She's begun to fuse with the Gilgamesh fetus.

00:05:02.450 --> 00:05:06.340
Her homeobox genes have broken down; she's becoming incapable of maintaining a human form.

00:05:08.250 --> 00:05:10.810
What on earth should we...

00:05:11.960 --> 00:05:14.690
Indeed, what should we do, I wonder?

00:05:28.170 --> 00:05:31.670
Now that she's like this, there's nothing for it but to keep watching till the end.

00:05:32.380 --> 00:05:34.370
These are consequences she herself invited after all.

00:06:07.950 --> 00:06:09.070
Ma'am...

00:06:14.490 --> 00:06:16.010
What is it this time?

00:06:17.360 --> 00:06:18.880
Come on, this way.

00:06:21.460 --> 00:06:22.520
You?

00:06:29.300 --> 00:06:32.600
Thanks for coming to visit us. We're glad you're here.

00:06:32.940 --> 00:06:37.370
It's not that I came because I wanted to; more like I have no place to go.

00:06:38.180 --> 00:06:41.240
I wonder who's gonna feed the fish from now on?

00:06:41.880 --> 00:06:43.210
The fish?

00:06:43.210 --> 00:06:50.320
They were Granddad's favorite, but big brother Kazamatsuri got really angry with me.

00:06:51.060 --> 00:06:55.250
He got so angry with me, even though I was being a good girl.

00:06:58.360 --> 00:07:00.130
What on earth happened?

00:07:00.770 --> 00:07:06.730
I made it so Granddad doesn't move, so he can't eat fish any more.

00:07:08.010 --> 00:07:09.270
I see.

00:07:10.210 --> 00:07:15.180
I want to go back to my home from before, but I don't know how to get there.

00:07:15.180 --> 00:07:18.220
I'm too scared of my big brother to really ask him.

00:07:18.220 --> 00:07:21.190
You were brought here by Kazamatsuri, right?

00:07:21.690 --> 00:07:22.710
Yeah...

00:07:25.420 --> 00:07:30.890
After I was adopted, big brother told me I could stay in the mansion forever.

00:07:33.600 --> 00:07:37.930
He took me into the big shiny bath.

00:07:44.580 --> 00:07:46.980
And he gave me pretty clothes to wear too.

00:08:00.360 --> 00:08:02.330
Then I met Granddad.

00:08:03.160 --> 00:08:04.690
Here, Granddad.

00:08:38.960 --> 00:08:40.790
How were your eyes at that time?

00:08:41.700 --> 00:08:44.770
I could see, until I had the operation.

00:08:44.770 --> 00:08:46.140
Operation?

00:08:46.140 --> 00:08:51.210
Little by little Granddad's eyes couldn't see anymore, because he's old.

00:08:51.210 --> 00:08:58.480
It seemed really inconvenient for him, and looking at him I felt sorry for him, and decided to give him my eyes.

00:09:03.320 --> 00:09:06.560
Even when I was little, I could see somehow even with my eyes shut,

00:09:06.560 --> 00:09:10.730
...so I thought it would probably be no trouble if I gave them to him.

00:09:10.730 --> 00:09:12.820
Because you have Dynamis after all.

00:09:15.830 --> 00:09:18.060
I don't understand that complicated stuff though.

00:09:18.740 --> 00:09:21.230
Did the Chairman also ask you to do it for him?

00:09:21.740 --> 00:09:24.710
Nope, he said there's no need to do that much.

00:09:25.940 --> 00:09:29.570
But I felt so, so sorry for Granddad.

00:09:30.010 --> 00:09:34.690
When I told him if I couldn't give them to him I'd quit being his adopted daughter,

00:09:34.690 --> 00:09:37.950
...my big brother came and said, "You'll be okay with this, right?"

00:09:39.860 --> 00:09:42.990
That's how they ended up letting me have the operation.

00:09:47.370 --> 00:09:53.600
Granddad said he could see his beautiful garden again; he was so happy.

00:09:55.810 --> 00:10:01.410
When I thought how it was my eyes he was seeing with, I was so, so glad.

00:10:29.810 --> 00:10:31.370
It was really a good thing.

00:10:34.780 --> 00:10:36.410
You love your Granddad, don't you?

00:10:37.050 --> 00:10:41.150
Yeah, when we're together I feel so at ease.

00:10:41.150 --> 00:10:42.640
I wonder why that is?

00:10:45.020 --> 00:10:46.390
It's strange, huh?

00:10:51.800 --> 00:10:54.920
I wonder what I should do from now on?

00:10:56.200 --> 00:10:58.400
I've lost my home and all.

00:10:59.800 --> 00:11:01.200
You can live here.

00:11:03.040 --> 00:11:04.370
Really?

00:11:04.780 --> 00:11:06.070
Yes...

00:11:11.380 --> 00:11:13.180
<i>Toru, you're listening, right?</i>

00:11:14.590 --> 00:11:15.620
Yes, Ma'am!

00:11:15.620 --> 00:11:18.150
<i>Show Reiko around the hotel.</i>

00:11:18.890 --> 00:11:20.020
Yes, Ma'am!

00:11:32.300 --> 00:11:35.910
When one thinks about it, the old days were a constrictive age, weren't they?

00:11:35.910 --> 00:11:40.080
With the decoding of the human genome, we came to know everything after all.

00:11:40.080 --> 00:11:44.100
What ailments we would suffer, what our natural lifespans were...

00:11:45.820 --> 00:11:51.380
In that old gentleman's case, he was aware that when he passed a certain age, he'd lose his vision.

00:11:51.820 --> 00:11:54.930
That was the reason he was so particular about those giant salamanders.

00:11:54.930 --> 00:11:57.220
It's said that eating them is good for one's eyesight, isn't it, my lady?

00:11:57.960 --> 00:11:59.830
It's no more than a superstition though.

00:12:00.770 --> 00:12:05.860
The ones he kept there were also transgenic, with genes recombined for breeding purposes.

00:12:06.300 --> 00:12:09.000
But to think Reiko actually gave him both eyes...

00:12:09.510 --> 00:12:12.670
It was likely at that man's instigation.

00:12:13.410 --> 00:12:14.250
My lady?

00:12:14.250 --> 00:12:17.850
In the old days, they'd exchange them for eyes made as cloned parts,

00:12:17.850 --> 00:12:20.250
...but with XX, it became impossible to do that.

00:12:21.120 --> 00:12:23.140
That's why he hunted down Reiko.

00:12:24.760 --> 00:12:28.160
I've assembled a body of data concerning Kazamatsuri, my lady.

00:12:28.790 --> 00:12:32.750
Just as you inferred, he is related by blood to the old gentleman Yuki.

00:12:33.100 --> 00:12:38.220
I had thought he was the one who might be a clone, but he's his actual son, is he?

00:12:38.900 --> 00:12:41.960
Yes, my lady, he's the child of one of Yuki's mistresses.

00:12:42.440 --> 00:12:47.840
Apparently the mother and her one child lived modestly, unacknowledged and without his support.

00:12:48.480 --> 00:12:52.810
But then he was bereaved of his precious mother during XX.

00:12:54.520 --> 00:12:59.220
The young orphaned Kazamatsuri was taken into the Yuki household.

00:12:59.860 --> 00:13:04.290
At that time, the old gentleman had also lost many blood relatives,

00:13:04.500 --> 00:13:07.870
...which is likely why he felt pity toward the boy, to whom he had blood ties.

00:13:07.870 --> 00:13:13.430
At first when he was taken in, due to the matter of his mother, it seems that he rebelled quite a lot.

00:13:15.440 --> 00:13:17.570
But that, too, shortly came to an end.

00:13:18.540 --> 00:13:21.950
The young Kazamatsuri, who was now living in the mansion,

00:13:21.950 --> 00:13:25.280
...received a new education as live-in student to the old gentleman Yuki,

00:13:25.420 --> 00:13:28.210
...and after reaching adulthood, he entered employment with the Mitleid Corporation.

00:13:29.250 --> 00:13:33.660
Likely as a result of his blood ties, his figure loomed larger and larger by degrees,

00:13:33.660 --> 00:13:37.250
...and he came to be regarded as the Chairman's successor.

00:13:38.000 --> 00:13:41.730
He appears to have undertaken some of the dirtier jobs of his own volition.

00:13:42.930 --> 00:13:49.110
His abilities were acknowledged, and he came to be entrusted with the subsidiary military contracting firm Equus.

00:13:49.110 --> 00:13:53.510
The formation of the Blattaria unit occurred after he assumed this post.

00:13:53.950 --> 00:13:56.750
Do you know the identity of those monsters?

00:13:56.750 --> 00:14:01.280
I was finally able to obtain evidence that elucidates that secret, my lady.

00:14:02.490 --> 00:14:06.550
This is the plant which produces the Blattaria, photographed some years ago.

00:14:07.190 --> 00:14:08.490
You've prepared well for this.

00:14:09.230 --> 00:14:10.320
It's kind of you to say so, my lady.

00:14:16.100 --> 00:14:17.600
What on earth is this?

00:14:17.600 --> 00:14:20.570
Sheep were used in place of pigs, but...

00:14:21.110 --> 00:14:22.870
They're also clones?

00:14:23.210 --> 00:14:25.340
Not ordinary clones, my lady.

00:14:25.340 --> 00:14:28.940
They were intended as weapons, their embryos created prior to XX.

00:14:29.450 --> 00:14:30.380
They can't be...

00:14:30.380 --> 00:14:32.610
Yes, they are transgenic, my lady.

00:14:33.220 --> 00:14:35.310
The same as those giant salamanders...

00:16:14.450 --> 00:16:17.080
The funeral's been held, so that should suffice.

00:16:17.790 --> 00:16:19.120
Rest in peace.

00:16:32.240 --> 00:16:38.340
Notify the authorities that a young girl wearing a kimono set fire to the mansion and fled.

00:16:43.680 --> 00:16:48.080
Hey, what happened to the older boy and girl who were always with you?

00:16:49.090 --> 00:16:50.920
Well, they kind of...

00:16:50.920 --> 00:16:52.020
Kind of what?

00:16:52.020 --> 00:16:55.550
More important than that, I'm going to show you a very special place.

00:17:00.500 --> 00:17:01.830
That's a nice sound.

00:17:02.970 --> 00:17:07.100
In this salon, there are lots of hard-to-get, valuable books.

00:17:07.740 --> 00:17:09.900
I can't read books.

00:17:10.110 --> 00:17:12.230
I'll read to you as much as you want.

00:17:13.410 --> 00:17:15.610
If you have a request, whatever it is, tell me.

00:17:19.450 --> 00:17:20.450
What's wrong?

00:17:20.450 --> 00:17:23.150
What could it be? What could this sound be?

00:17:24.120 --> 00:17:25.280
Wait!

00:17:27.060 --> 00:17:28.460
It's from down there.

00:17:29.230 --> 00:17:30.720
This place is kind of...

00:17:38.170 --> 00:17:40.330
It's here. It's here!

00:17:43.910 --> 00:17:45.380
Sorry, this girl...

00:17:45.380 --> 00:17:46.410
Shh!

00:17:46.410 --> 00:17:50.610
It's from here. I can hear some kind of sound from here.

00:18:00.160 --> 00:18:02.250
It sounds like a girl.

00:18:02.790 --> 00:18:05.160
"Ta... tsu... ya..."

00:18:09.370 --> 00:18:10.700
She's saying, "Tatsuya."

00:18:16.510 --> 00:18:17.880
Hear anything yet?

00:18:17.880 --> 00:18:19.210
Nope...

00:18:21.210 --> 00:18:22.410
How about you?

00:18:22.410 --> 00:18:24.010
I can't hear anything.

00:18:24.280 --> 00:18:26.120
Can you really hear that?

00:18:26.120 --> 00:18:27.950
There'd be no point lying, right?

00:18:30.960 --> 00:18:33.480
That's my big sister.

00:18:35.960 --> 00:18:38.120
What's my sister saying?

00:18:39.130 --> 00:18:43.830
She says, "Tatsuya... we'll always... stay together."

00:18:45.270 --> 00:18:50.100
"We won't be lonely or anything. We won't be lonely."

00:18:50.910 --> 00:18:52.030
Kiyoko...

00:18:56.880 --> 00:18:57.910
Kiyoko...

00:18:58.350 --> 00:18:59.610
Kiyoko...

00:19:03.290 --> 00:19:05.280
So you're still alive, then?

00:19:06.490 --> 00:19:07.650
You are, aren't you?

00:20:10.650 --> 00:20:12.380
Oh, it's Mr. Kazamatsuri!

00:20:14.560 --> 00:20:16.320
Mr. Kazamatsuri!

00:20:16.730 --> 00:20:18.090
Mr. Kazamatsuri!

00:20:18.500 --> 00:20:21.530
You guys have a good, hearty meal before work.

00:20:21.530 --> 00:20:22.660
Yes, Sir!

00:20:23.400 --> 00:20:26.470
I've put you through nothing but hard experiences.

00:20:26.470 --> 00:20:28.340
But this is a time of trials.

00:20:28.810 --> 00:20:31.980
A contemptible terrorist and the monsters who are his minions...

00:20:31.980 --> 00:20:34.440
...have driven people into the furthest depths of fear.

00:20:35.210 --> 00:20:37.410
Annihilating them is our mission.

00:20:38.680 --> 00:20:42.310
Do not forget that this is a just war to defend liberty and peace.

00:20:43.990 --> 00:20:46.680
The hard fighting will likely go on and on.

00:20:47.090 --> 00:20:49.120
But we will win!

00:20:49.560 --> 00:20:50.790
Without fail, we will win!

00:20:51.360 --> 00:20:57.160
To restore peace and order to the world, and to build an era of fresh hope!

00:23:24.920 --> 00:23:27.540
Dad is trying to destroy the world,

00:23:28.190 --> 00:23:31.580
...this time completely, by means of a Cleansing Flood.

00:23:32.390 --> 00:23:35.920
I don't really understand it, but it seems he's going to do something to the sky again.

00:23:36.660 --> 00:23:40.030
He says by doing so, he's going to give birth to a new human race.

00:23:40.800 --> 00:23:42.960
He says it's because we're in the way.

00:23:43.330 --> 00:23:45.160
He says it's because there's no value in us going on living.

00:23:46.000 --> 00:23:49.300
But it's all right; we'll always stay together, Tatsuya.

00:23:49.640 --> 00:23:51.470
We won't be lonely or anything.

00:23:51.980 --> 00:23:53.370
We won't be lonely.
